<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00TF">Proposition <span data-tag="00TF">11.6.0.221</span>.</a> Let $f: X_{} \rightarrow S_{}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The morphism $f$ is a right fibration. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every pair of integers $0 &lt; i \leq n$, every lifting problem 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \Lambda ^{n}_{i} \ar [r]^-{\sigma _0} \ar [d] &amp;  X_{} \ar [d]^{f} \\ \Delta ^{n} \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur]^-{\sigma } \ar [r]^-{ \overline{\sigma } } &amp;  S_{} } \]
</div>
<p>
 admits a solution (indicated by the dotted arrow). 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article>
